      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under medical supervision. The 1,600 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and the analgesic and anti-inflammatory benefit doesn't increase.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the usual maximum for conditions like rheumatologic pain.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day). This is a common dose for analgesia.\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, if that was the intended daily amount, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
      }
     ],
